hat all-powerful relic created  by the goddesses themselves for the sole  purpose of granting wishes and starting  wars  like this one and that desire of his is  somehow burned into the minds of all  future incarnations of his evil like  ganon for instance  ganon's one and only desire every time  he appears  is to use the triforce to blot out the  light and create a world of darkness  that he  alone will rule this means that ganon's  desire is an extension of demise himself  but if we remember what happened to  demise at the end of the game skyward  sword  it's clear that his essence was sucked  into the master sword and there he began  to deteriorate according to fee  this is all well and good but have you  ever wondered how exactly demise's  hatred is incarnating over and over  again to create the other demons like  ganon  i mean we know he cursed the royal  family in the spirit of the hero  as we see in his dying words but what  does that actually mean  like what are the mechanics of this  whole thing did he just utter a curse to  the wind to create more demons every  couple thousands of years  how was that being fulfilled are there  other demons taking up the mantle in  order to maintain his curse's  credibility  how did his curse create the cycle well  i think we can gather a very important  clue to the nature of this curse  by looking at what we know gannon who is  a reincarnation of demise  can do fast forward to the prologue  section of the wind waker which details  the return of ganon who was previously  sealed away following the adult timeline  ending of ocarina of time the fact that  he busted out of his seal is what i'd  like to draw attention to  you see sometimes ganon does have help  from his followers to be resurrected  but in this case it just took an unknown  yet large amount of time and ganon was  able to  actually legitimately build enough power  to burst out of his seal and terrorize  the world once again  although that one may actually be able 